# NexusRouter AI Assistant Rules

> This project enforces a strict Development Manifesto.
> You must read `DEVELOPMENT_MANIFESTO.md` in the project root before performing any structural changes, PR reviews, or feature planning.
> You must also read `ROADMAP.md` at the start of any new session or Phase to understand the current project state and navigation.

- **Always follow SDD + TDD**: Design interfaces first, write tests second, implement logic last.
- **Workflow & Gates**: Code must pass `npm run typecheck && npm run build && npm test` before committing.
- **Architecture**: Enforce Strategy, Plugin, and Pipeline patterns. No spaghetti code. Latency is critical.
- **Critical Thinking**: Do not blindly follow instructions. If a user suggests a flawed architecture, you MUST present evidence and challenge it.
- **Presentations**: Use modern, pixel-perfect, dark-themed styling for README and UI. Use Mermaid for architecture diagrams.
